# patch: 005-command-hooks-chunked
# format: CHUNKED ONLY (2.1.242+). Monolithic keeps 005-command-hooks.patch.
# version: authored against 2.1.260
# depends: none
# description: Appends __commandHooks custom commands to the builtin slash
#              command table.
#
# WHERE IT MOVED: commands.js DOES NOT EXIST on a chunked tree. The builtin
#   command table is inside services/compact/precomputedCompact.js (the 9.1 MB
#   merged chunk), at the tail of the array builder, ~line 225390.
#
# ANCHOR: the monolithic patch keyed on `...remoteWebCommands,` — an ANCHORED
#   name that DOES NOT RESOLVE on chunked trees (measured: zero occurrences of
#   `remoteWebCommands` anywhere in the 2.1.260 tree). The replacement landmark
#   is the STRING LITERAL in the same array, `...kJ('logout'),`, which is unique
#   tree-wide; the `'logout'` literal survives minification, though the function
#   wrapping it does not (it is `Qee` on 2.1.259 — measured), so that call
#   appears only as CONTEXT and never on an added line.
#
# The added line introduces NO minified name: it references only
#   globalThis.__commandHooks
# and is inserted at the array tail, after the trailing `...[],` spreads, so it
# cannot change the relative order of any upstream command.
#
# ⚠️ COVERAGE NOTE: this patch is exercised by no automated check here. A
#   headless `-p` turn never renders the slash-command list, so a green turn
#   test says nothing about it; it applies cleanly and is syntactically carried
#   into the bundle, but "custom commands actually appear in the REPL menu" is
#   BELIEVED, not verified.
